# ── Generator rules ──

@rule element-protons
real: rule
says: an atom's proton count is its element number; neutrons give isotopes (content/physics.dnat)

@rule element-paint
real: rule
says: any natural element can be painted into the world from the element tree; lab-made ones (93 and up) unlock once a civilization first creates them

@rule element-chemistry
real: rule
says: elements combine by their chemistry into compounds, minerals, air and the molecules of life

@rule element-abundance
real: rule
says: hydrogen and helium are by far the most common elements in stars and giants; rocky worlds are mostly oxygen, silicon, iron and magnesium

@rule element-heavy
real: rule
says: heavy elements are made in stars and supernovas and spread by them; young galaxies have fewer of them
